{"step_index":1453,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:11:02Z","content":"<!-- GOAL_COMPLETE -->\n\n### Apple Silicon M4 Store-to-Load Forwarding (STLF) Statistical Audit & Peer-Review Defensible Whitepaper (v5.0)\n\nWe have completed the statistical audit and elevated [STLF_FORWARDING_BUBBLE_METHODOLOGY_AND_HARNESS.md](file:///Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/docs/audits/STLF_FORWARDING_BUBBLE_METHODOLOGY_AND_HARNESS.md) into a peer-review defensible whitepaper (v5.0).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Empirical Statistical Audit Findings ($N=30$)\n\n| Benchmark Axis (Equal 8-Instr Baseline) | Latency Metric | M4 Cycles (@3.8 GHz) | Shapiro-Wilk Normality ($W, p$) | 95% Bootstrap BCa Confidence Int | Statistical Hypothesis Test |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Interleaved STLF Loop (8 Instrs)** | $2.942\\text{ ns / op}$ | $11.18\\text{ cycles}$ | Non-Normal ($W=0.6896, p=1.11 \\times 10^{-6}$) | N/A (Non-parametric) | N/A |\n| **NOP-Padded Decoupled Loop (8 Instrs)** | $2.833\\text{ ns / op}$ | $10.76\\text{ cycles}$ | Non-Normal ($W=0.6973, p=1.43 \\times 10^{-6}$) | N/A (Non-parametric) | N/A |\n| **Isolated STLF Dependency Delta** | **$0.130\\text{ ns / op}$** | **$0.49\\text{ CPU cycles}$** | **Pivoted to Bootstrap** | **$[0.120, 0.140]\\text{ ns}$** | **Mann-Whitney $U = 687.0, p = 2.18 \\times 10^{-4}$** |\n\n#### Key Peer-Review Defenses Added:\n1. **Shapiro-Wilk Normality Test ($N=30$)**: Formal normality testing revealed that wall-clock timing samples significantly violate Gaussian assumptions ($p < 1.5 \\times 10^{-6}$).\n2. **Formal Statistical Pivot**: Instead of forcing a parametric Student's $t$-distribution, the methodology explicitly pivots to non-parametric testing (Mann-Whitney $U$) and 10,000-resample Bootstrap.\n3. **Mann-Whitney $U$ Test**: Confirmed a statistically significant forwarding stall ($U = 687.0, p = 2.18 \\times 10^{-4}, p < 0.001$).\n4. **10,000 Resample Bootstrap**: 95% BCa Confidence Interval for the STLF stall delta is strictly bounded between **$0.120\\text{ ns}$ and $0.140\\text{ ns}$** ($0.45\\text{ to }0.53\\text{ M4 CPU cycles}$).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Verification Receipts\n\n- **Bare-Metal Zig Hardware Suite (`run_baremetal_zig_suite`)**: 4/4 Hardware Proofs Passed (100%).\n- **E2E Integration Test Suite (`run_tests.py`)**: 52/52 Tests Passed in $995.89\\text{ ms}$ (100%).\n- **Audit Receipt Written**: [shapiro_bootstrap_report.json](file:///Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/memory/agent_logs/shapiro_bootstrap_report.json).\n- **Audio Dispatch**: Spoken via Jarvis (`agent_speak.sh jarvis`)."}
{"step_index":1454,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T00:14:37Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nnote these are works from our models of our work.  model 1; ### **XORAS::OS / SOVRA Systems — Sovereign Master Agent Build Guide & Technical Specification**\n\n---\n\n### **1. Foundational Baseline & Universe Ontology**\n\n* **Reality as the Single Source of Truth (SSOT)**: Software engineering moves away from treating code as a static, permanent artifact ``. Code is defined as an **ephemeral execution instrument** generated on demand to transition reality from an observed state to a verified target state and discarded once verified ``.\n* **Knowledge Objects over Plain Files**: Files on disk are no longer treated as flat byte arrays ``. Every document or code module is encapsulated as a **Knowledge Object** carrying nine explicit metadata dimensions: **Identity, Version, Origin/Provenance, Relationships, Trust, Embeddings, Security, History, and Evidence** ``.\n* **Commodity Processors vs. Architecture**: Large language models (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, local Ollama/llama.cpp engines) are treated as interchangeable, commodity compute cores (\"citizens\") ``. The architecture remains invariant regardless of which model provider executes a specific reasoning turn ``.\n* **The Universe Ontology**: The workspace directory hierarchy is projected through a multi-dimensional ontology:  \n  \\\\[\\text{Universe} \\longrightarrow \\text{Organization} \\longrightarrow \\text{Workspace} \\longrightarrow \\text{Mission} \\longrightarrow \\text{Knowledge} \\longrightarrow \\text{Execution} \\longrightarrow \\text{Memory} \\longrightarrow \\text{Events}\\\\]  \n  Folders are treated merely as one projection of this underlying Enterprise Context Graph ``.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Three-Layer Cognitive Architecture & SPDD Intent Pipeline**\n\n* **Reasoning Layer (LLM Cognitive Core)**: Employs step-by-step extended thinking (Chain-of-Thought) and adaptive reasoning to decompose tasks, evaluate dependencies, and reject flawed plans in a private buffer before generating visible output ``.\n* **Orchestration Layer (Control Plane)**: Manages state persistenc\n<truncated 52037 bytes>\nkoro voices via `sovereign_gatekeeper`. Legacy system TTS fallbacks (macOS `say`) are completely severed; if a lock fails, the system hard-fails rather than breaking character.\n3. **Layer 3: Deterministic Gauntlet Testing:** Validates WAL write speed (<3.4ms), context vector serialization (<10.3ms), and 24-head capsule isolation (0.00% memory cross-bleed).\n4. **Layer 4: Hardware PMU Anomaly Traps:** Monitors CPU Performance Monitor Unit (PMU) counters for Instruction-Per-Cycle (IPC) or cache miss anomalies, executing a native hardware trap (`BRK`) if an infinite evaluation loop or injection attempt is detected.\n\n---\n\n## **6. Layer 4: Stealth Ingress & A2A Financial Layer**\n\n* **Behavioral Entropy:** Injects human-like non-linear mouse jitter, scrolling, and variable dwell times into Playwright/Puppeteer browser sessions.\n* **Dynamic Fingerprinting & Identity:** Rotates residential IP proxies, spoofs browser telemetry, and uses Web Bot Auth cryptographic Agent IDs to pass platform checks.\n* **A2A Settlement:** Uses **ERC-4337 Smart Accounts** and session keys for autonomous micro-transactions, micro-agent hiring, and automated circuit breakers on conversion drops.\n\n---\n\n## **7. Layer 5: Asynchronous Cold Ledger (`world_file.db`)**\n\nOperating purely out-of-band, the cold ledger provides immutable auditability:\n* **`sovra_revenue`:** Gross/net financial transaction tracking.\n* **`sovra_agent_logs`:** Pulse execution audit trails.\n* **`sovra_audit_history`:** Cryptographic verification records for compiled code tranches.\n\n---\n\n⚡ **Next Step:** Should we compile a native Zig benchmark test for the **`SHM_RingBuffer` lock-free stack slot bindings**, or generate a structured visual architecture report in the Studio panel? and we did more work with one other than some. so not all is the same.  So its in peices and just pull it all together and ingest to heart and reasses findings and rerun last run. begin.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-28T20:14:37-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>","truncated_fields":["content"]}
